Ladybird preserves important custom properties when later normal
declarations name the same property in a parsed block. The last value
wins among declarations with the same priority. CSSOM setProperty()
continues to replace the value and priority unconditionally.

Blink’s FilterProperties() places important declarations last, then
visits declarations in reverse order and keeps each custom-property
name only once. WebKit’s filterProperties() also visits declarations in
reverse order, with a pass for important declarations before normal
ones. Gecko’s PropertyDeclarationBlock::push() keeps an important value
when a normal declaration names the same property. These approaches
all preserve the last declaration at the highest priority.
